w: ||On her nest,|with her young,|Sat the Star- ling in the|stee- ple,|
 c3/2 c/ B B | A A !breath!G2 | F/ G/ A/ G/ A A | ^c A z2 | %10
w: While be- low the|great bell swung|To the church to call the|peo- ple.|
"^poco accel." d3/2 =c/ B/4 B3/4 A3/4 G/4 | D2 D z | G/ A/ B/ A/ G/ !breath!G3/2 | !>!d3 z | %14
w: ”Mo- ther, mo- ther,” cried the|star- lings,|”What is that? oh mo- ther,|tell!”|
"^a tempo" ^c A =c A | ^c A =c A | z!<(! A/ F/ d d | !breath!f4!<)! | c A B G | A F G !breath!C | %20
w: “Don’t be fright- ened,|lit- tle dar- lings,|'Tis the great church|bell,|Ring- ing out its|so- lemn warn- ing,|
 F/ G/ A/ G/ A A | !breath!c4 |"^sempre cresc." c3/2 c/ B B | A A G !breath!C | %24
w: That the peo- ple far and|near|All may know 'tis|Sun- day morn- ing,|
 F/ G/ A/ G/ A/ A3/2 | !breath!^c4 |"^dolce cantabile" d3/2 =c/ B/ B/ A/ G/ | D2 D z | %28
w: And make haste to ga- ther|here.|While the or- gan’s sweet- ly|play- ing|
!pp! G/ A/ B/ A/ G G | d3 z |"^cresc." ^c A =c A | ^c A (=c !breath!A) |!<(! F/ G/ A/ F/ d2-!<)! | %33
w: Lit- tle birds need have no|fear!|While be- low the|folk are pray- ing,|You can sing your hymns|
 !breath!d2 a2 | f4- | f4- | f z z2 | z4 |] %38
w: _ up|here!”|_|||
